I'll be straight with you: about 14 hours of study from zero cloud experience is very unlikely to be enough for an associate-level architecture exam — these exams expect you to reason about many services and design trade-offs, which usually takes weeks of study plus hands-on practice.
Your options:
• reschedule the exam by 4–8 weeks, if the exam's rescheduling policy allows it — I'll check the current policy and any fees;
• study more hours per day for the next two weeks (still risky);
• sit the exam as planned and treat it as a practice run (costly if the fee isn't reimbursed on a fail).
One question: is the October date fixed by your company, or was it your own choice?
